7. Protected disclosures

Nothing in these terms prohibits disclosures protected by applicable law,
including reporting suspected legal violations to a government authority or
making a protected confidential disclosure to legal counsel. No prior notice
to Mindclade, LLC. is required where applicable law prohibits such a
requirement.

U.S. trade-secret immunity notice. Under 18 U.S.C. § 1833(b), an individual
will not be held criminally or civilly liable under federal or state
trade-secret law for disclosing a trade secret: (a) in confidence, directly or
indirectly, to a federal, state, or local government official or to an
attorney, solely to report or investigate a suspected violation of law; or
(b) in a complaint or other document filed under seal in a lawsuit or other
proceeding. An individual who files a retaliation lawsuit may disclose the
trade secret to their attorney and use it in the proceeding if any document
containing the trade secret is filed under seal and the trade secret is not
disclosed except by court order. This notice does not authorize otherwise
unlawful access to or acquisition of the Materials.

